// FIELD SERVICE — AUSSENDIENST — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// FIELD SERVICE as Kraftwerk, circa The Man-Machine and Computer World — a game
// alternate of plumber, selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk.
// Außendienst is German for field service.
// 
// The machine plays the plumber's song: a sequencer arpeggio that never stops, a
// Minimoog bass on a 3-3-2 figure, dry electronic drums, a Simmons snare, metal hats,
// the Casio pi-po and Kraftwerk blips on the off-sixteenths. The hook on a plain square
// with a music bell over it, a vocoder singing it at half speed, a Polymoog choir, and
// a robot on six bits saying the name of the job. No risers and no pump: the style is
// precision, repetition, and parts entering one at a time.
// 
//   1–4    the sequencer, the blips, "field service" (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–8    + the Minimoog bass and a kick on one and three
//   9–16   the kit; the hook at half speed on the square, A then B
//   17–24  the hook at its own speed, square and bell; choir; the vocoder answers
//   25–32  the pocket calculator: kit out, the pi-po plays the hook's rhythm
//   33–40  bridge: F C Am G, the C phrase half speed on the vocoder, strings, E home
//   41–56  everything: A A B B A A C C, the robot every eighth bar
//   57–64  the machine winds down; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
// The two robot lines are this song's own voices (voiceParams), compiled from text by
// work/local/_kw-speak.mjs the way the desk compiles a spoken phrase.
// 
// 64 bars at 116. Written by work/local/_fs-remix-aussendienst.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): the machine winds down: each part stops on a cut (57–64), and the last bar loops itself quieter and quieter.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
